## 4. Live Activity controls not working from Dynamic Island / Lock Screen
- **Bug #1 — Buttons unresponsive:** `PausePetTimeIntent`, `ResumePetTimeIntent`, `StopPetTimeIntent` conformed to plain `AppIntent` instead of `LiveActivityIntent`, so tapping them from the Dynamic Island/Lock Screen didn't reliably execute. Fixed by switching conformance to `LiveActivityIntent` (one-word change per intent, in `AppIntent.swift`).
- **Bug #2 — Live Activity stopped appearing at all (Simulator):** `PetTimeActivityManager.start(...)` had a single combined `guard` with no logging, so if `ActivityAuthorizationInfo().areActivitiesEnabled` was `false` (likely the Simulator's Live Activities toggle being off under Settings → Dr. Paw), it failed completely silently — no console output, no UI, no error. Fixed by splitting the guard into two, each with a distinct `print`, so the exact cause now surfaces in the console. Diagnosis confirmed it was a Simulator-testing constraint (no Apple Dev account on that Xcode install), not a code regression from the Bug #1 fix — you were told to check the console output after rebuilding to confirm which of the three logged cases you hit.

